5|0@Aquariums^1439063630#ctw6r3i:VitaP$:Something I've found that really helps is to emphasize, if you don't work on comission, that you really don't care about selling for selling's sake. Also using metaphors that people can emotionally understand, like "Imagine living your life in a jail cell as opposed to an apartment or house. Sure, you can do it, but there's a difference between living and living happily. That's one of the ways of looking at this betta's tank options." Of course, then you get the guy who comes in and says, "Well if this one dies I'll just flush it lol." But for the most part, it does work! A lot of people want what's best for their pets, it's just with fish some people don't realize how much awareness their little guys have.
