17|0@Aquariums^1439060411#ctw54lc:pseud0nym$:&gt; "Don't release that fish into a lake." You realize that is a criminal offense right? You also realize that invasive fish from aquariums cause billions of dollars in damage right? They just had to serialize an entire lake in California because the goldfish killed everything else. Armored catfish (common plecos) are causing massive shoreline erosion threatening homes and businesses. Walking catfish are a plague in Florida. No, do not release that fish into a lake. The moment you put it into a tank, you are responsible for that animal until you either rehome it, it dies or you euthanize it. Do not release ANYTHING from an aquarium into the water in the wild. That includes plants and even the water from the tank. 
