7|0@Aquariums^1439060546#ctw572u:pseud0nym$:You add salt to freshwater aquariums to keep the fish healthy. It does nothing of the sort (not talking about ich treatment). What it does is make nitrite less toxic and the idea behind adding it was you could go longer between changing the water so you could maximize the goodness in your "seasoned" water (at least that myth has finally died for the most part). 
3|0@Aquariums^1439061299#ctw5kr2:boomsloth$:You can use it (if you know what you're doing) when keeping many aquatic amphibians or raising amphibian eggs. But yeah it only acts to prevent fungus. 
