1|0@Aquariums^1439151703#ctx7295:Snakeman94$:Yeah I'm not saying anything bad on people who keep big fish, it's awesome if I had the room and money of course I'd get me a tank big enough for a red tailed cat and other big daddy fish. What i am saying that is bad when you get the people who overcrowd the big fish. Working at a petstore you come across a lot of good people, but also a lot of ass holes who shouldn't be trusted with a pet rock! There's a guy who comes in our store that has a 75 gallon tank that has a like foot long black pacu, two oscars, a jack Dempsey, a red devil, three red belly piranhas, and maybe a parrot cichlids and some plecos. This kinda crap is ridiculous. He showed me a pic of the tank acting all proud and I haut felt awful. All those big fish that should have tons more room:/ I've told the guy multiple times how wrong it is but he could care less. To top it all off, the guy got 150 feeder goldfish. The water looked awful and the fish looked sickly. Just awful and doing this is sertainly a form of animal abuse
2|0@Aquariums^1439082181#ctwf6w9:VitaP$:Nah. From my perspective if you keep a culture that you're personally monitoring, awesome. I've got a guppy and shrimp culture going, and I'd love to get another few running. Waste not, want not. It's more along the lines for me of "Feeders from places you trust, and don't get upset if your fish get sick, because unless you quarantine feeders you buy or receive, it's probably going to happen."
