3|0@Aquariums^1439097068#ctwm6ed:amberlynns$:- "Having a filter means I don't need to clean the tank!" - "Bettas live in tiny puddles and so they prefer living in tiny bowls." My biggest pet peeves are probably the people who assume fish in pet stores are fully grown and those who choose to house fish in small bowls/tanks when they KNOW how large the fish should grow. A woman I know bought a 2.5g plastic tank, filter, preset heater, and two juvenile Blood Parrots. She was made fully aware that it wasn't acceptable for multiple reasons and she couldn't care less. Those of us who love the hobby may seem snobbish, but we care about fish like everyone else cares for dogs and cats. All we ask is that people research the hobby and the fish they want to buy before actually diving in. If you can't provide a proper home/environment for an animal, you shouldn't get one. Simple as that.
